{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0923"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge nature/ecology","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/nature__ecology.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",283],["+"," Visitors always notice the same oddity: the giant's forelimbs are only about as long as a human's arms, absurdly short for an animal that, by some estimates, needed more than 20 tonnes of meat a year, yet they were heavily muscled and ended in two clawed fingers."],["=",750]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",271],["+"," Den Besuchern fällt stets dieselbe Merkwürdigkeit auf: Die Vorderbeine des Riesen sind nur etwa so lang wie die Arme eines Menschen, absurd kurz für ein Tier, das nach manchen Schätzungen mehr als 20 Tonnen Fleisch im Jahr brauchte, doch sie waren kräftig bemuskelt und endeten in zwei bekrallten Fingern."],["=",694]]}]},
